# Security Must-Nots

- Never rely on client-side checks for authorization — every table needs RLS policies for SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.
- Never expose the Supabase service role key or other secrets to client bundles; never commit `.env*` (except `.env.example`).
- Never trust request input: parse with Zod in Server Actions and Route Handlers before use.
- Never fetch user-provided URLs without validation (SSRF); never redirect to unvalidated URLs.
- Never log PII or tokens; avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless the content is escaped/serialized.

Full checklist (API, auth boundaries, uploads, rate limits): skill `veta-security-owasp`; Supabase client and RLS usage: skill `veta-supabase-rls`.
